      "system": [
        "Caller-provided initialized filter state, covariance, measurement/update masks and process/control settings",
        "Consistent units, frames, measurement timing and rclcpp Time/Duration values",
        "C++ toolchain and generated package interfaces required by the reviewed CMake configuration"
      ],
      "notes": "correct selects finite measured dimensions, takes the absolute value of negative covariance diagonals, floors very small diagonal variances at 1e-9, computes a Kalman gain by matrix inversion, normalizes angular innovation, applies a Mahalanobis threshold and updates state/covariance using the Joseph form. predict builds an Euler-angle transfer function and analytical Jacobian, calls inherited control preparation, optionally computes dynamic process noise, projects state/covariance and wraps state angles. It uses 1/cos(pitch); numerical conditioning and singularity behavior were not tested. These methods mutate filter internals and can emit configured debug output; this file defines no main, ROS subscriptions/publishers or physical robot command. CMake places src/ekf.cpp in rl_lib and separately builds ekf_node from another source that was not read in this bounded review. CMake selects C++17 for non-WIN32 builds. Package version 3.8.3 and ROS Index jazzy-devel metadata are declarations, not tested ROS, OS, architecture, Python or sensor compatibility. A fetched file alone is insufficient."
    },
